{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.mu3_ne_multiplicative_cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.mu3_ne_multiplicative_cluster","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L171-L180","doc":"**(WALL, modularity form.)**  `μ₃ > 0` cannot equal any multiplicative\nproduct-decrease cluster.  Companion to `mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster`; the two\nprove the same exclusion from the two viewpoints (product content ≤ 0 vs.\nsupermodular Δ²g ≥ 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_cluster_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_cluster_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L160-L169","doc":"**Multiplicative ⇒ non-positive cluster.**  The product-decrease block-trace's\nconnected 3-body cluster is `≤ 0` (for `E₀ ≥ 0`): it lands on the supermodular /\n`c₃ ≤ 0` side, so it can never equal `μ₃ > 0`.  Modularity-language re-derivation\nof `QOU.MassTheory.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_supermodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_supermodular","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L150-L158","doc":"**Multiplicative ⇒ supermodular.**  With `g₀ > 0` and decrease factors\n`r_a, r_b ∈ [0,1]`, the product-decrease block-trace has `Δ²g ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_second_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.multiplicative_second_diff","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L144-L148","doc":"For a product-decrease block-trace, `Δ²g = g₀·(1 − r_a)·(1 − r_b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.mu3_requires_submodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.mu3_requires_submodular","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L126-L134","doc":"**`μ₃ > 0` forces submodularity.**  If the positive residual moment `μ₃`\nequals the connected cluster `c₃` (with `E₀ > 0`), then the joint block-trace is\nstrictly submodular (`Δ²g < 0`).  This is the exact reframing of the standing open\nsign question: μ₃ is reachable by the joint-trace cluster **only** in the\nsubmodular regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster_pos_iff_submodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster_pos_iff_submodular","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L112-L124","doc":"**The door, as an iff.**  With `E₀ > 0`, the connected cluster is positive\n**iff** the second mixed difference is negative — i.e. iff the joint block-trace\nis strictly **submodular**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster_eq_neg_second_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster_eq_neg_second_diff","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L103-L108","doc":"**The cluster is minus `E₀` times the second mixed difference.**\n`c₃ = −E₀·Δ²g`.  This is the whole content: the connected 3-body cluster sign is\nthe (opposite of the) modularity sign of the joint block-trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.cluster3","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L98-L101","doc":"The connected 3-body cluster of the joint block-trace,\n`c₃ = joint − pair_sum = E₀·(g_a + g_b − g_∅ − g_ab)` (the framework's\n`three_body_joint_trace_a3` object). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.secondDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3ClusterModularity.secondDiff","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3ClusterModularity.lean#L91-L96","doc":"The **second mixed finite difference** of a set-function `g` on the interface\nBoolean lattice `{∅, a, b, ab}`, represented by its four values\n`(g_∅, g_a, g_b, g_ab)`:  `Δ²g = g_ab − g_a − g_b + g_∅`.  `Δ²g > 0` is\n**supermodularity** (co-present bonds reinforce), `Δ²g < 0` is **submodularity**\n(diminishing returns). ","signatureChunk":0}]}